{"Passing request.filters as a third argument to applyTemplateVariables deviates from the standard DataSourceApi signature which typically only accepts (target, scopedVars) - need to verify LokiDatasource has been updated to handle this third argument": 0.3285868465900421, "Interpolating the query before calling querySupportsSplitting causes a regression where the $__range variable is replaced by a static time value, making the isQueryWithRangeVariable check always return false for interpolated queries, leading to queries being incorrectly split when they should remain whole": 0.7196473479270935, "datasource.applyTemplateVariables may mutate the query object, which can cause side effects if the request object is reused for retries or by other plugins - the query object should be cloned before passing to the interpolation method": 0.26026755571365356, "Redundant interpolation occurs because runShardSplitQuery interpolates targets at the start, then calls splitQueriesByStreamShard which eventually calls runSplitQuery which also performs interpolation, resulting in applyTemplateVariables being called multiple times for the same targets": 0.7187900543212891}